<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arikesari Maravarman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">7th century</span> · Also known as Koon Pandiyan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arikesari Maravarman was a king of the early medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandya dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madurai">Madurai</a> in the later 7th century. Shaiva tradition holds that the saint <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sambandar">Sambandar</a> converted him from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jainism">Jainism</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaivism">Shaivism</a>, an episode associated with the rise of the Bhakti movement in Tamil country. He extended Pandya power against neighbouring rulers.</p></div>
